The subject line starts with "Any advices for a middlegame ..."

In fact, learning to manage skills slots is a middle game goal for
any class.  In the early game it's tempting to #enhance any
weapon class any time you get told you feel more configent.  In
the short run doing so makes your combat effectiveness better
so it appears to improve your game.

But appearances can be decieving and that's a powerfull lesson
of the middle game.  It's SO easy to die on turn 30,000 because
on turn 5,000 you #nhanced the wrong weapon.  But who ever
thinks in those terms?  I died of this hoard of critters swarming
me not of some action ten levels ago, right?  Uhn, not really
right.  There's what you died of, but there's also what you did
that got you into that situation.

Early game is to learn inventory management.  What to drop
where you found it (packrat says - nothing but rocks and buolders
;^), what to drop in piles per level, what to take to your main
stash.  Middle game is to learn skill slot management, among
other skills.



